;; Clojure's eval level's divergences from its reference (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP1, RPS3,
;; RPS16): the classes every non-pass of the level's checks falls into, in the format of
;; test/goi/divergences.edn. A case's class is the first whose :match finds its "RESULT REASON":
;; - Clojure's suite (test/arbace-go-results.edn against upstream's, test/baseline-results.edn: every
;;   assertion passes upstream), one case per test or namespace that does not pass or does not run:
;;   "skip NS: why" (a namespace not run), "skip NS/TEST: why" (a test not run), "fail NS/TEST (fail
;;   F, error E)", "error NS/TEST (fail 0, error E)"; test.generative's "fail spec S", "error load NS";
;; - the oracle (test/oracle/known-go-amd64-frozen.edn, the eval level's files): "known REASON", the
;;   known mismatch's reason.
;; :kind :design (by design, decided) or :deferred (to be built, named where); :decided where the
;; decision is recorded, :pending when it is recorded nowhere (the user's to decide). bin/reap
;; judges it (test/reap/main.ae); bin/clojure-tests --divergences judges a run of the suite.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 ;; the suite: namespaces and tests that do not run
 {:id :out-for-good
  :title "XML (SAX), gen-class, Java serialization, Swing/AWT, classes from jars"
  :kind :design
  :why "out of the Go build for good: arbace.xml's SAX, gen-class (and its AOT-compiled examples), ObjectOutputStream, java.desktop (java.awt.Color, java.awt.Point, arbace.inspector's Swing), tools.deps' jars (arbace.repl.deps)"
  :decided "doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6, \"Not to be done (the user, 2026-10-10)\"; doc/go/EVAL-NOTES.md, \"The suite's last failures\""
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.(clojure-xml|genclass|genclass\.examples|serialization|repl\.deps): "
          #"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/(test-bean|test-dot|test-proxy-non-serializable): "]}
 {:id :javadoc-url
  :title "java.javadoc's javadoc-url-test: java.sql.Connection is not in the Go build"
  :kind :design
  :why "javadoc-url-test's java.sql.Connection assertion errs at Class/forName: java.sql is not in the Go build's world (D6). Its other two errors (Class.getModule) are fixed: jrt's java.lang.Module (RPS55 (a), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"As built: RPS55\"; doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Modules\")"
  :decided "doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6; RPS55 (a): the java.sql assertion by design (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): RPS40-RPS59\")"
  :match [#"^error clojure\.test-clojure\.java\.javadoc/javadoc-url-test \(fail 0, error 1\)"]}
 {:id :class-files
  :title "class files: the Go build writes and reads none"
  :kind :design
  :why "compile writes no class files and ASM is gone (clj-1208 loads a deftype AOT-compiled from compilation.load-ns; test-proxy-method-order reads the proxy's class file with ASM)"
  :decided "doc/STANDALONE-SURVEY.md D13; doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 23"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/clj-1208: " #"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/test-proxy-method-order: "]}
 {:id :xml-stream
  :title "javax.xml.stream (reflect's invoke-checks-accessibility)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the test reflects over javax.xml.stream's classes, which are not in the Go build's world (java.xml)"
  :decided "RPS5 (a), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md (deferred)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.reflect/invoke-checks-accessibility: "]}
 {:id :seq-and-transducer
  :title "speed: transducers' seq-and-transducer (200,000 test.check trials)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "about 8.6 ms a trial on the evaluator, beyond the 900 s a namespace may take; EC7 (its timeout) not taken"
  :decided "RPS5 (a), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md (deferred: speed); doc/go/SPEED-NOTES.md, EC7"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.transducers/seq-and-transducer: "]}
 ;; the suite: tests that fail
 {:id :q1-boxed-prims
  :title "the evaluator's fns are boxed (Q1): no primitive interfaces"
  :kind :design
  :why "a fn made at run time is one Go type calling invoke, not invokePrim: it implements none of IFn's primitive interfaces (IFn$LL, IFn$LOL ...), so no recur-mismatch warning, no \"Cannot coerce long to int\", and a ^long fn of the REPL is no IFn$LL (the suite's compilation tests; the oracle's native.ae cases)"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-PLAN.md, Q1 (a) (the user, 2026-10-09)"
  :match [#"^fail clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/(primitive-return-decl|incorrect-primitive-type-hint-throws) "
          #"^known By design \(doc/go/EVAL-PLAN\.md, Q1"]}
 ;; the oracle's known mismatches (eval)
 {:id :locales
  :title "locale data: root and English only"
  :kind :design
  :why "the shipped build's locale data are java.base's root and English alone (JRT_LOCALES defaults to none); another language takes the root's data, where the JVM has jdk.localedata's"
  :decided "the user, 2026-10-11; doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Text and locales\", TM4, TL5"
  :match [#"^known The shipped build's locale data are java\.base's root and English alone"]}
 {:id :security-providers
  :title "security providers: SUN and SunJCE only"
  :kind :design
  :why "java.security's other ten providers are not in the Go build and fail to load, as a provider the JDK cannot find"
  :decided "doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Security\", SC4"
  :match [#"^known The providers of the Go build are SUN and SunJCE"]}
 {:id :serialization
  :title "Java serialization"
  :kind :design
  :why "java.io.ObjectOutputStream is not in the Go build (the proxy itself works)"
  :decided "doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6, \"Not to be done (the user, 2026-10-10)\"; doc/go/ORACLE.md, Exclusions"
  :match [#"^known Out of the Go build for good \(B1-PLAN's D6"]}
 {:id :security-manager
  :title "java.lang.SecurityManager not in the world"
  :kind :design
  :why "JEP 486: the Security Manager is permanently disabled and nothing of the program names the class, so (resolve 'java.lang.SecurityManager) is nil; RT's default imports dropped it"
  :decided "doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 11"
  :match [#"^known java\.lang\.SecurityManager is not in the Go build's world"]}
 {:id :identity-hash
  :title "identity hashes (not reproducible)"
  :kind :design
  :why "the JVM recorded HotSpot's identity hash of a StringBuilder, a per-thread xorshift sequence"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-NOTES.md, phase 2B (as decided for #object printing)"
  :match [#"^known Not reproducible, as decided for #object printing"]}
 {:id :main-since-v4
  :title "main's divergences from the frozen reference (v4)"
  :kind :design
  :why "the oracle's reference is arbace-for-java-26-v4's jar; main names two ambiguous MultiFn classes in the order of their names (ac8b9718), and its loaders look for .ae first (the .ae rename), so its not-found message names .ae"
  :decided "doc/STANDALONE-NOTES.md, \"S4: the oracle's reference\"; commit ac8b9718; the .ae rename (2026-10-11)"
  :match [#"^known Divergences of main from the frozen reference"]}
 {:id :method-invoke-message
  :title "a message's wording: Method.invoke on a receiver of another class"
  :kind :design
  :why "jrt's Method.invoke words it as JDK 26's DirectMethodHandleAccessor does ('object of type java.lang.Long is not an instance of java.lang.String'), the JVM Arbace's call 'object is not an instance of java.lang.String'; the exception's class is the same. Recorded as a known mismatch only: by design or to align the message is the user's (RPS19)"
  :decided "RPS19 (a), by design (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-24): RPS18-RPS29\")"
  :match [#"^known Message: a qualified method value \(String/\.indexOf\)"]}
]
